            <p class="text-gray-500">Source of the "94% goes to millionaires" claim. State-by-state revenue estimates.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-4">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-800">State legislation</p>
            <p class="text-gray-500">
              <a href="https://www.oregon.gov/dor/pages/2026-summary-of-legislation.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-800 underline">Oregon DOR 2026 summary ↗</a> ·
              <a href="https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Measures/Overview/SB1507" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-800 underline">OR SB 1507 ↗</a> ·
              <a href="https://lims.dccouncil.gov/Legislation/B26-0457" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-800 underline">DC B26-0457 ↗</a> ·
              <a href="https://app.leg.wa.gov/billsummary?BillNumber=6229&Year=2025&Initiative=false" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-800 underline">WA SB 6229 ↗</a> ·
              <a href="https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/2026RS/fnotes/bil_0001/hb0801.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-800 underline">MD HB 801 ↗</a>
